{
  "reports": [
    {
      "title": "Auxiliary Power Loss at Synthetic East Substation after Composite Splice Fault",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "The splice connector at Synthetic East joined an aluminium barrel to a stranded copper conductor.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Galvanic corrosion formed a brittle oxide wafer at the dissimilar metal interface over years.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": [0]
        },
        {
          "text": "The cable pit lacking drainage kept several centimetres of water around every splice.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "No lightning discharge did strike the site; a capacitor bank switching transient did arrive.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The transient voltage caused a small sparkover in the water layer at 14:32.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [1, 2, 3]
        },
        {
          "text": "The sparkover decomposed a track of the ethylene-propylene cable insulation into carbon.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [4]
        },
        {
          "text": "The carbon track eventually bridged phase and earth, and a full ground fault started.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [5]
        },
        {
          "text": "The phase-to-earth fault current reached 11.4 kA on the 33 kV feeder bay.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [6]
        },
        {
          "text": "The feeder differential relay detected the increasing current imbalance within three cycles.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [7]
        },
        {
          "text": "One pole of the circuit breaker opened, disconnecting Synthetic East from the grid.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "After the breaker trip the 33 kV bus de-energised, stopping supply to the auxiliary transformer.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The auxiliary transformer loss cut all HVAC power to the control room's switchgear.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [10]
        },
        {
          "text": "The battery charger stopped charging, so the 220 V DC substation battery carried the entire load.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [11]
        },
        {
          "text": "After 45 minutes, the DC bus voltage had decayed from 243 V to 201 V.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "The low-voltage lockout prevented the tie switch motor from closing the emergency feed.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [13]
        },
        {
          "text": "In 2025 the planned splice thermal scan had been deferred but not cancelled.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "At 16:08 a hired 500 kVA mobile generator was connected to the essential 400 V board.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [14]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operating staff used the temporary generator to power the battery chargers and control loads.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [16]
        },
        {
          "text": "After the generator ran, one repair crew replaced the splice with a copper compression connector.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [17]
        },
        {
          "text": "The pit was fitted with drainage pipe and a partial-discharge monitor was wired to the alarm.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [18]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Auxiliary Power Failure at Synthetic West Substation Caused by Excavation Damage to Cable",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "The 11 kV cable at Synthetic West had no protective concrete slab above its route.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A detailed drawing claimed an 80 cm depth, but the actual cable was buried at 42 cm.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Planting trench plans were made without checking the subsurface utilities register of any kind.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "No lightning discharge occurred; nevertheless, the live cable was struck by an auger bit.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The auger's cutting tooth deeply gouged the cable's lead sheath and wrappings.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [3]
        },
        {
          "text": "Moisture from the wet soil easily reached the cable's exposed paper insulation.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [4]
        },
        {
          "text": "The moisture allowed an electrical conduction path, and the phase insulation broke down into a ground arc.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [5]
        },
        {
          "text": "The cable current swelled to 3.2 kA and tripped the overcurrent relay after a short time.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [6]
        },
        {
          "text": "The overcurrent relay sent a trip signal to the circuit breaker at the feeder's remote end.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [7]
        },
        {
          "text": "The circuit breaker opened, cutting off the 11 kV supply for station auxiliary power.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "The station battery charger then lost its AC source, and the DC bus started to fall.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The essential lighting switched to emergency lamps that were not designed for full duty.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [10]
        },
        {
          "text": "Data terminal displays flickered when the DC control voltage dipped to 104 V.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [10]
        },
        {
          "text": "Two motorised disconnector controls refused to act because the undervoltage lockout engaged.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "The transformer hall temperature reached 41 °C as cooling fans stayed stopped.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [10]
        },
        {
          "text": "The site supervisor relied on grass appearance instead of locating cable before work.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A 200 kVA mobile generator, brought from a nearby store, fed the essential AC bus at 16:45.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [14]
        },
        {
          "text": "With temporary power available, workers tested the cable and found the auger cut location.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [16]
        },
        {
          "text": "They removed the damaged length and jointed in a new 11 kV cable with a cold-shrink splice.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [17]
        },
        {
          "text": "Concrete covers, sand layers, and marker tape were placed at the corrected burial depth.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [18]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
